        "original_id": "22d6e225-c5dc-506c-9679-fc090747608b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: New Hampshire Route 118, Woodstock, Canaan, White Mountains Region, Upper Valley region, Cushman, Berlin, Maine border, Dorchester, New Hampshire, Dorchester Common Historic District\n- Buildings: Dorchester Community Church, town hall\n\nFacts:\n- New Hampshire Route 118 stretches from Woodstock in the White Mountains Region south to Canaan in the Upper Valley region.\n- The northern boundary of the White Mountains Region begins at Cushman, runs to Berlin, and then goes east to the Maine border.\n- The Dorchester Community Church is a historic church building located off New Hampshire Route 118 in Dorchester, New Hampshire.\n- The Dorchester Community Church was built in 1828 in the Dorchester Common Historic District.\n- A town hall was built in 1844 in the Dorchester Common Historic District on the site of the town's first 1828 town hall.",
